Using StressTest.Scala we simulate 50 requests to /run-simulation with each 
request asking the server to print an unique number i (1 to 50).

With a non-thread-safe structure, several problems could occur:

- lost log entries
- corrupted internal state
- inconsistent log sizes
- exceptions during iteration
- duplicated or partially written entries

Example failure:

Thread x and Thread y both try to append at the same moment:

Initial size = 10

Thread x reads size = 10
Thread y reads size = 10

Thread x writes at index 10
Thread y also writes at index 10

Result:

One message disappears (overwritten)
The size counter becomes incorrect (might show 11 instead of 12, or be completely inconsistent)
The log content becomes corrupted

Which would lead to us having less than the 50 logs after the program ends.